## §4 verdict
  Published by the arm: 23
  B (arm's population, re-driven at line level): 23
  delta: +0

  POST-HOC 6 IS RETRACTED. The arm did not under-count. Its published 23 is reproduced
  EXACTLY once its own population rule is applied alongside its selector. The +4 post-hoc 6
  reported as a miss is the arm's own four fixture patterns, which the arm excluded
  deliberately so as not to join the population it grades.

  THE DEFECT WAS MINE AND ITS SHAPE IS WORTH THE NAME: I copied the selector line
  byte-for-byte, asserted that provenance in §0 of two scripts, and that assertion made the
  reconciliation FEEL reproduced while the population silently differed. A byte-identical
  selector in a wider population is a different instrument, and it fails by accusing the
  other figure rather than by going quiet.

